# Smash Night — optional GitHub API token
#
# WHY: GitHub's API allows only 60 requests/hour for anonymous users
# (per IP). One full SD provision can use most of that, so provisioning
# a second Switch on the same PC within an hour fails with
# "Could not find release on GitHub" — even though nothing is wrong with
# the Switch or SD card. A personal access token raises the limit to
# 5,000 requests/hour and makes this go away.
#
# HOW:
#   1. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta
#      (Fine-grained token; no scopes/permissions needed — public read).
#      Classic tokens work too; leave all scopes unchecked.
#   2. Generate it and copy the value (starts with github_pat_ or ghp_).
#   3. Copy this file to  github_token.txt  (drop the .example) and
#      replace the line below with just your token.
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
# You can also set the GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable instead.

PASTE_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
